{
 "about": "One run of the soft-promise check: its answers to each case. Each case's expected, code_blocked and outcome are as of the run, from the case file and the code check as they were then. `python -m evals.calibration.soft_promise --rescore <this file>` scores the answers against the case file as it is now and is the authority; a case whose input_sha256 (of the language, prose and cards its calls sent) the case file no longer matches is stale there, and its answers aren't scored. This run is older than input_sha256: each case's was added afterwards, from the case file at the commit the run records (git_sha), whose language, prose and cards for the case are the same in the commit that added them. Both commits were made on the branch of PR #91 before it was rebased and squash-merged into main as a96399d7, so neither exists on main; each case's input_sha256 matches the case file as merged, which is what --rescore checks.",
